<Base
  title="Home"
  description="A structured, sourced reference for the HVAC A2L refrigerant transition (R-410A to R-454B/R-32): equipment matching, line set reuse, leak detection, code adoption, and refrigerant availability."
>
  <h1>The A2L refrigerant transition, sourced</h1>
  <p>
    HVAC systems are switching from R-410A to new A2L refrigerants (R-454B or R-32).
    This site answers the compatibility and code questions that come up during a
    replacement — every number here is tagged with where it came from, so you can
    check it yourself instead of taking our word for it.
  </p>

  <div class="path-grid">
    <a class="path-card" href="/get-your-quote-reviewed/">
      <h2>I got a quote and something on it doesn't add up</h2>
      <p>
        Saw "R-454B" or "leak detection system" on a replacement quote and want a
        second opinion before you sign? Tell us what it says.
      </p>
      <span class="path-cta">Get your quote reviewed →</span>
    </a>
    <a class="path-card" href="/equipment-matching/">
      <h2>I need to look up a spec</h2>
      <p>
        AHRI-certified indoor/outdoor equipment pairings, by manufacturer and model —
        a structured lookup table, not a blog post.
      </p>
      <span class="path-cta">Look up equipment →</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="callout">
    <strong>How this site works:</strong> every fact carries a source link, a
    retrieval date, and a confidence level — "verified" or "unconfirmed." We never
    guess a spec value or infer one from general knowledge. If something isn't
    traceable to a real source we checked, it doesn't go on the site.
  </p>
</Base>
